From 7c177bd252d0c0be94932eeb5c83319853ddc0d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 01:58:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02986/11362] [outer-loop] conductor claude bridge: default
 model -> Opus 4.8 (ultracode tier) for every claude call

Operator directive: set the conductor's claude -p bridge to ultracode effort + Opus 4.8.
Recon finding (2-agent workflow w4cr7zu03): the bridge ALREADY hard-codes --effort max (the CLI
ceiling, >= ultracode's xhigh; 'ultracode' is not itself an --effort value per claude --help 2.1.177)
and planner/retro ALREADY pin claude-opus-4-8 via systemd AGENT_MODEL_PLANNER/RETRO. The ONLY gap:
DEFAULT_MODEL_BY_TYPE['claude'] was 'sonnet', so non-planner/retro claude calls (requires_claude_verified
experiments, the audit-script default) fell back to Sonnet. Flipped to claude-opus-4-8 so the WHOLE
claude bridge is Opus 4.8. Planner/retro unaffected (model_override > default). Effort unchanged at max.
NOTE: dynamic-workflow-orchestration (the other half of interactive 'ultracode') does NOT apply to a
single headless claude -p call -- only the reasoning-effort + model carry over; that is inherent to -p
mode, not a setting. Takes effect on the next conductor restart (currently mid-A6, do not interrupt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 scripts/research_conductor.py | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/research_conductor.py b/scripts/research_conductor.py
index 368be50f3e..93a881a14f 100644
--- a/scripts/research_conductor.py
+++ b/scripts/research_conductor.py
@@ -61,7 +61,14 @@ AGENT_BIN_BY_TYPE = {
     "codex": os.environ.get("CODEX_BIN", "codex"),
 }
 DEFAULT_MODEL_BY_TYPE = {
-    "claude": "sonnet",
+    # 2026-06-20 operator directive: the claude -p bridge uses Opus 4.8 (the ultracode
+    # tier) for EVERY claude call. Planner/retro already pin claude-opus-4-8 via the
+    # systemd AGENT_MODEL_PLANNER/RETRO env; this makes the DEFAULT for any other
+    # claude-typed call (e.g. requires_claude_verified experiments, the adversarial
+    # audits' own default) Opus 4.8 too, instead of Sonnet. Effort is hard-coded
+    # --effort max on the claude argv below (max is the CLI ceiling, >= ultracode's
+    # xhigh effort; 'ultracode' is not itself an --effort value, per claude --help).
+    "claude": "claude-opus-4-8",
     "gemini": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview",
     "opencode": "opencode/big-pickle",
     "codex": "gpt-5.5",
